# Line endings — SCOPED DELIBERATELY, added 2026-08-05 (#382).
#
# This machine has core.autocrlf=true globally. cmd.exe reads batch files in the OEM code page and
# mis-parses LF-only files — it re-reads and loops. Measured while writing a wrapper that has since
# been removed: 2.5 MB of "'his' is not recognized" before it was killed. tools/make_portable.cmd
# has carried the ASCII half of that warning in its own header for months; this is the LF half, and
# it is here so the next .cmd added to the repo does not have to re-learn it.
#
# KEEP THE PATTERNS NARROW. A broad `* text=auto` would renormalize every tracked file on the next
# checkout — a whole-repo line-ending diff across three worktrees that merge into each other. The
# cost of that lands on a merge, where it is hardest to read.

tools/*.cmd  text eol=crlf
# For any shell script added later: sh chokes on the \r, and autocrlf would supply one.
tools/*.sh   text eol=lf
